{
  "id": "Compound::DB00674 - Gene::57053",
  "verbalization": "Galantamine, a cholinesterase inhibitor, is implicated in the interaction with the acetylcholine-activated Cation-selective Channel Activity through its binding to Chrng and Chrne, which are both involved in the same biological process. The evidence suggests that Galantamine modulates the activity of these channels, which in turn influence the function of Chrna10. The final scores from the three paths indicate a consistent and significant relationship between Galantamine and Chrna10, with the mechanism involving the inhibition of a channel that is part of the acetylcholine signaling pathway. The overlapping roles of Chrng and Chrne in the same pathway support the idea that Galantamine's effect on these proteins leads to a downstream impact on Chrna10. The integrated evidence highlights a mechanistic link between Galantamine and the function of the nicotinic acetylcholine receptor subunit Chrna10, mediated through the modulation of ion channel activity.",
